# Glossary — {{ project_name }}

Tier 1. Link on first use in docs.

- **fast loop** — per-commit background review (roborev); findings accrue in a
  ledger until fixed.
- **slow loop** — scheduled or on-demand deep review writing to
  `docs/reviews/`; includes the retro section that proposes deterministic
  replacements for repeated AI usage.
- **shrink** — converting repeated AI usage into deterministic tooling.
- **layer** — one concern of the agentic layer (environment, isolation,
  orchestration, LLM deps, loops, tasks, enforcement, attribution).
- **agents.toml** — project-scoped dotagents manifest: pinned skills,
  subagents, MCP servers. The machine-readable dependency list for agents.
- **experiments log** — `docs/experiments.md`; entries tagged `[variable]`
  (the thing under test) or `[harness]` (a deliberate change to relative
  constants).
{% if include_git_ai %}
- **git-ai** — line-level AI attribution; agent checkpoints produce
  authorship notes. See `docs/how-git-ai-works.md`.
{% endif %}

